  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{4,8,\u2026,20},{24,28,32,36},{40,44,\u2026,56},{60,64,\u2026,80}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{4,8,20},{24,28,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because the elements $12$ and $16$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{4,8,\u2026,20},{60,64,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because the elements $24,28,\u2026,56$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,\u2026,20},{22,24,\u2026,58},{60,62,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $A.$\n\n- ${{4,6,\u2026,20},{24,26,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $6$) that do not appear in $A.$",
